Audio samples ship in two sets, under two different terms.


Samples/ — the TR-808 sounds
----------------------------

Derived from the Roland TR-808 Sound Sample Set 1.0.0 (1994) by Michael
Fischer, as published by the TidalCycles project under the Creative Commons
CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication:
https://github.com/tidalcycles/sounds-tr808-fischer
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

The files here were trimmed to their transient, resampled from 44.1 kHz to
48 kHz in the frequency domain, normalized, and written as 24-bit stereo.
CC0 imposes no conditions, so no attribution is required; it is recorded
here because knowing where a sound came from is worth more than the licence
requires.


Samples/ — the glass sounds
---------------------------

glass_break, glass_shatter and glass_tap are generated rather than recorded:
inharmonic partials, a filtered noise transient, and scattered grains for the
debris tail. Part of this project and covered by its LICENSE.
